/-!
# Interacting functional Schrödinger evolution and continuum measurement

This module constructs the configuration-local interacting sector that was missing between the
Ipek--Caticha functional generator and the repository's measure-theoretic Born rule.

For a measurable configuration space `(X, μ)`, positive `ℏ`, and measurable real free and
interaction energies `E₀` and `V`, it defines

`U(t)ψ(x) = exp(-i t (E₀(x) + V(x)) / ℏ) ψ(x)`

on `L²(X, μ)`. The construction proves the group law, exact norm conservation, strong continuity,
and the pointwise interacting Schrödinger equation. A normalized `L²` state then defines the
actual probability measure `|ψ|² μ` using `Measure.withDensity`. Deterministic measurable readouts
push this probability measure forward, while stochastic detectors compose it with an arbitrary
Markov response kernel. The shared continuum entropic-clock infrastructure proves that unitary
configuration-local evolution conserves the Born-measure clock, while detector channels contract
distinguishability and monotonically recover the associated complex-action amplitude. Stochastic
detectors compose exactly, yielding a monotone clock chain through cascaded measurements. A supplied
positive-time Markov response semigroup then gives actual detector-time outcome dynamics, an antitone
stationary-reference clock, nonnegative additive interval production, and a complex-weight Lyapunov law.
Its weakly continuous extension supplies initial bounded-observable recovery, a right observable-generator
interface whose stationary outcome laws have zero generator, and a nonnegative right clock-production
rate whenever that rate limit exists. The concrete identity detector preserves every outcome law;
for any stationary outcome the zero production rate is constructed and every supplied rate is uniquely zero.

## Scope

The interaction is a real configuration-local multiplication potential in a representation where
the Hamiltonian is diagonal. This is a genuine interacting infinite-dimensional `L²` evolution,
but it is not a diagonalization theorem for arbitrary functional differential Hamiltonians and is
not a construction of renormalized interacting QFT. The detector carriers are classical measurable
readouts or Markov response kernels; a quantum instrument, amplification, environment-induced
decoherence, and a detector-pointer Hamiltonian are separate dynamical layers.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

