zil_file_contract physlib.ipekCatichaInteractingFunctionalMeasurement where
  promises "A measurable real free-plus-configuration-local interaction energy constructs an explicit unitary C0 functional Schrodinger group on L2 of an arbitrary measured configuration space. Every normalized state constructs an actual Born probability measure. Deterministic readouts and arbitrary stochastic Markov-response detectors construct outcome laws; unitary evolution preserves them, while response channels contract the KL clock and compose exactly. Under supplied positive-time Markov detector dynamics with stationary reference, the Caticha outcome clock is antitone, interval production is nonnegative and additive, and the calibrated complex-action modulus is monotone. A weak-C0 detector extension recovers initial bounded-observable expectations, places stationary outcome laws in the kernel of any identified weak generator, and makes every existing right clock-production rate nonnegative. The concrete identity detector preserves every outcome law; stationary outcome laws construct a zero right rate and any stationary rate is uniquely zero."
